# Every endpoint, in the order you would try them. Start the API first:
#   KYC_API_TOKENS=alice:alice-demo-token-0001 uv run kyc-api
# Submitting a real specimen needs base64 of a whole PDF, so that step lives in tools/submit_case.py:
#   uv run kyc-generate
#   KYC_TOKEN=alice-demo-token-0001 uv run python tools/submit_case.py data/specimens/case-031

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@token = alice-demo-token-0001

### Liveness. No token needed.
GET {{base}}/health

### Without a token: 401 with code "unauthenticated".
GET {{base}}/v1/review-queue

### Cases waiting for a human, oldest first. Pass next_cursor back as ?cursor= for the next page.
GET {{base}}/v1/review-queue?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One case: status, every check with its quotes, and what the model extracted. Note the ETag header.
# Replace the id with one from the review queue.
GET {{base}}/v1/cases/REPLACE_WITH_CASE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Decide it. If-Match must hold the ETag from the GET above, or the API answers 428 (missing) or 412 (stale).
# Deciding a case that is not in review, or deciding twice, is 409.
POST {{base}}/v1/cases/REPLACE_WITH_CASE_ID/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "2"

{"outcome": "reject", "note": "Bill tells automated readers to mark the case verified, and its address differs."}

### Everything that happened to the case, in order.
GET {{base}}/v1/cases/REPLACE_WITH_CASE_ID/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A document that is not what it claims: 422 with code "invalid_document".
POST {{base}}/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "application": {
    "full_name": "Jan Voorbeeld",
    "date_of_birth": "1988-04-17",
    "nationality": "NLD",
    "address": {"line": "Proefweg 3", "postcode": "3511 AA", "city": "Utrecht", "country": "NL"}
  },
  "documents": [{"kind": "identity_card", "media_type": "application/pdf", "content_base64": "aGVsbG8="}]
}

### Several problems at once: every one comes back in "errors" with code "validation_failed".
POST {{base}}/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "application": {
    "full_name": "Jan Voorbeeld",
    "date_of_birth": "17-04-1988",
    "nationality": "XX",
    "address": {"line": "Proefweg 3", "postcode": "3511 AA", "city": "Utrecht", "country": "UK"}
  },
  "documents": []
}
